      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good point, I think originally we was not factoring in the boosted task utilization...\n\nHowever, it seems not correct to check against a new_util value which factors in the min_util. That\u0027s because we do not flag overutilized a system based on the boosted utilization, but only the actual utilization.\n\nI agree that this check should be done right after L6778, but only for !prefer_idle tasks... or we should probably better refactor the meaning new_util to be just \"wake_util + task_util(p)\", while at L6785 we should use the max clamping to update the value of \"min_util\" itself... and then fix all the usages in the code we have by checking to use the proper variable.",
